<Layout title="Evidence & attribution">
  <div class="wrap page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Portfolio / Editorial principles</p><h1>A clear account<br />of the work.</h1><p class="lead">Technical credibility depends on the difference between what I implemented, what a team delivered, and what I hope to investigate next.</p></div>
  <article class="wrap prose standalone"><h2>Professional accounts</h2><p>Engineering case studies draw on my supplied career dossier and reconciled content strategy of 1 November 2026. These are professional accounts, supported by private working material where available. They are not presented as independent public audits.</p><h2>Individual and shared contributions</h2><p>Each case study states my role. Co-developed mechanisms, team delivery, external consultancy, and individual implementation are distinguished. A platform name in the integration index is a context for work, not a claim that I built its entire integration.</p><h2>Sanitised technical explanations</h2><p>Customers are anonymised. Diagrams express general engineering ideas using original conceptual workflows. They do not reproduce employer source code, infrastructure, database schemas, customer records, credentials, internal endpoints, or security incidents.</p><h2>Outcomes and measurements</h2><p>Conflicting record counts, unreconciled throughput claims, financial impact, and company-wide scale figures are excluded. Proposed validation checks are labelled as recommendations; they are not historical test evidence.</p><h2>Research and recognition</h2><p>The e-banking paper has a public bibliographic record and DOI. Experimental ML work, exploratory collaboration, and future healthcare AI interests have separate labels. Recognition is based on my supplied academic record, with authentic certificates still to be prepared for public presentation.</p><h2>Independent lab and writing</h2><p>The membership sandbox and technical notes were created for this portfolio. They use synthetic examples and are educational demonstrations. They do not expose production code or imply deployment at my employer.</p></article>
</Layout>
